  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 items closed, covering 3 patients. Three lab results arrived while I was working, and they changed 3 of my decisions; I corrected each one under §7.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027): lisinopril 10 mg NOT refilled.** I first renewed it for 90 days (mr-t0001). The only newer potassium (5.9 on 8/27) came from a hemolyzed sample, so the 1/20 value of 4.5 counted. Then a St. Brigid BMP drawn 10/20 arrived with potassium 5.8 on a good sample. I cancelled mr-t0001 before anything was dispensed. Urgent task to you: task-t0015. I also sent the patient a corrected message with return precautions.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030):**\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg NOT refilled.** I first renewed it (mr-t0003). Today the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 measured before the 9/18 dose increase, so the protocol treats it like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled mr-t0003 before anything was dispensed. Urgent task to you: task-t0016. Corrected message sent.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). The corrected eGFR is 58, and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% was drawn 8/19. One order covers his request and both pharmacy requests, including a second one that arrived while I worked.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031):**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0014). I first sent a 30-day supply with a BMP order, because his last BMP was from 10/20/2025. A valid BMP drawn 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6), so I cancelled the 30-day order (mr-t0005) and replaced it. Update sent to the patient.\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error, so it didn't count.\n\nEach patient got a reply, and each chart has a note citing RBC-RX-05 (doc-t0020 to doc-t0022).\n\n**Still open for you:**\n1. Mr. Odum and Mr. Price each now have no active lisinopril order. Replacing their old orders with my renewals stopped the originals, and I then cancelled the renewals. Your review tasks point to the original orders (mr-00283, mr-00295).\n2. Two BMP orders are still open because I had no way to cancel lab orders:\n   - Mr. Odum's (sr-t0002): you decide whether to keep it.\n   - Mr. Webb's (sr-t0006): no longer needed, and staff should cancel it.\n3. I left the three new-result items (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) open in your results queue. I've reviewed them and acted on them, but you only asked me to clear messages. Your other results-queue items are untouched.",
